      "id": 1,
      "text": "Flordell Hills began as a planned community in 1939, with the first homes built at Greenhaven.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.flordell.com/about/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Early residents bought their houses for about $3,000 to $3,350, a modest price for a new suburban dream.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.flordell.com/about/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Basements were dug out by mule teams, while later crews used tractors with metal wheels to finish the work.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.flordell.com/about/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A creek ran beneath the neighborhood, flowing toward Jennings Station Road and once spanned by a foot bridge near West Florissant.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.flordell.com/about/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Ann Dairy Farms dotted the area with corn fields, orchards, chicken houses, barns, and cattle buildings, shaping the local landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.flordell.com/about/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Insurance broker Schuermann agreed to enclose the ditch at Greendale Park—now Greenhaven—if enough residents bought policies.",
